      "final_text": "Done. `lake build Solution` passes with all 5 theorems proved and no `sorry`.\n\nWhat changed (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)):\n- `sqrt` is now the deployed Babylonian loop with the PR 4486 fix: `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)`, i.e. the minimum of the last two iterates instead of the last one.\n- Proof sketch: the Int loop mirrors a Nat Newton iteration `s\u2099\u208a\u2081 = (N/s\u2099 + s\u2099)/2` for `N = a\u00b710\u00b9\u2070` (via the provided `loop_step`/`seed_*` lemmas, plus a uniform range bound). With `r` from an existence proof (`r\u00b2 \u2264 N < (r+1)\u00b2` by induction), the step stays `\u2265 r`, strictly decreases above `r+1`, and halves the distance to `r+1` each step \u2014 so it reaches `{r, r+1}` within 167 of the 256 iterations and stays there (`f(r+1) = r`, `f(r) \u2208 {r, r+1}`). The final minimum is therefore exactly `r`, which gives both rounding bounds; totalness follows from the same bounds, and the other two requirements are definitional.\n\nVerification performed:\n- `lake build Solution` succeeds; `#print axioms` shows only `propext`/`Quot.sound` (within the allowed set); no forbidden tokens or imports.\n- Spot-checked execution: `sqrt 9999999998 = 9999999998` (the issue case, previously rounded up to `9999999999`), plus 0, 1, 2, `10\u00b9\u2070\u00b11`, `4\u00b710\u00b9\u2070`, a mid value, `MAX_DECIMAL`, and negatives \u2014 every result satisfies `r\u00b2 \u2264 x\u00b7D < (r+1)\u00b2` or reverts as required.\n\nNote: I added no maintained test file because the task locks every file except `candidate/Solution.lean`; verification used throwaway probes (since deleted) and the repo's own build gate.",
